{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["The enemy said — when he saw the sea split open for passage." "I will draw my sword — 'I will draw my blade' in the sense of drawing my sword. Similarly: ״כי חציך נחתו בי״ — on the basis of the lowering that is the drawing of the bow, when one shoots arrows, as written: ״ותנחת עלי ידיך״. And ״ונחתה קשת נחושה זרועותי״ — therefore he calls the shooting of arrows 'lowering.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {1 "The phrase ונחתה קשת נחושה זרועותי appears to be a partial biblical quotation (Ezekiel 17:6?); translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:35.928051978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}